<title>USA: Seagate Technology Inc Q1 earnings summary.</title>
<headline>Seagate Technology Inc Q1 earnings summary.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTS VALLEY, Calif. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>SEAGATE TECHNOLOGY, INC.</p>
<p>				  FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS</p>
<p>		 (In Thousands Except Per Share and Percent Data)</p>
<p>						    Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						    Sep 27,	 Sep 29,</p>
<p>							1996	 1995 (1)</p>
<p> Net sales				   $2,060,825    $2,140,805</p>
<p> Gross profit				   392,776	 396,100</p>
<p> As a percent of sales			  19.1%	   18.5%</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		 179,668	 173,441</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes		  50,307	  52,632</p>
<p>Net Income:</p>
<p>   Amount					 129,361	 120,809</p>
<p>   As a percent of sales			 6.3%	    5.6%</p>
<p>Net income per share:</p>
<p>   Primary					   1.18	    1.22</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				   1.06	    1.05</p>
<p>Number of shares used in</p>
<p>per share computations:</p>
<p>   Primary					109,698	  99,062</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				129,333	 124,774</p>
<p>(1) The three month period ended September 29, 1995 has been restated to reflect the merger with Conner Peripherals, Inc. on a pooling of interests basis.  </p>
<p>(2) During the latest quarter, the company reversed about $9.6 million of its restructuring accrual, which was offset by about $9.5 million in other non-recurring merger-related costs incurred during the period.</p>
<p>Year ago first quarter results include a one time writeoff of in-process research and development of $2.8 million incurred in connection with the acquisition of Sytron Corp. Without that writeoff and its related tax effect ,fully diluted net inome per share for the year-ago quarter would have been $1.07.</p>
